            "text/html": "<marimo-accordion data-labels='[&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eData provenance and chemistry audit&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;,&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eWhat the bounds mean\u2014and what this lab cannot establish&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;,&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eAI use, contribution, and reproduce this notebook&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;]' data-multiple='false' data-expanded='[]'><div><div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Source: <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/openadmet/openadmet-expansionrx-challenge-data\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ExpansionRx / OpenADMET full release</a>.\nDataset DOI: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.57967/hf/9687\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">10.57967/hf/9687</a>.\nLicense: <strong>CC BY 4.0</strong>. Credit: Expansion Therapeutics and the OpenADMET Consortium.\nMeasurements and structures are redistributed unchanged when embedded; the decision annotations are this notebook's additions.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>SHA-256:</strong> <code>f674ec74cca1146bc386f832a32d4b8d921d3c312f92cb436cc005901c724a3c</code>.\nIdentical repeated source rows removed: <strong>0</strong>.\nThe parser checks IDs, expected columns, qualifiers, and non-finite or malformed values;\nambiguous schemas and conflicting repeated IDs stop execution for inspection.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">RDKit parses the published SMILES and preserves stereochemistry in depictions.\nMulti-fragment IDs are retained and flagged: <strong>0</strong>.\nNo salt stripping, tautomer merging, or averaging of repeated assays is performed.\nPublished salts and tautomer forms may encode assay-specific context we cannot reconstruct;\nunspecified stereochemistry remains unspecified. No stereoisomer is invented.\nDistinct canonical isomeric structures: <strong>7617</strong>;\nstructure groups with multiple IDs: <strong>1</strong>.\nThese grouped structures remain separate published IDs, so their decisions are not independent samples.</span></span><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>All parsed source IDs (7,618):</strong></span></span><marimo-ui-element object-id='mMqW-0' random-id='179f4c36-2371-a278-4b71-03ee90485d6b'><marimo-table data-initial-value='[]' data-label='null' data-data='&quot;[{&#92;&quot;Endpoint&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Kinetic solubility&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;exact&#92;&quot;:7298,&#92;&quot;censored&#92;&quot;:125,&#92;&quot;missing&#92;&quot;:195,&#92;&quot;unparsed&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;invalid&#92;&quot;:0},{&#92;&quot;Endpoint&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Human microsomal clearance&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;exact&#92;&quot;:4542,&#92;&quot;censored&#92;&quot;:279,&#92;&quot;missing&#92;&quot;:2796,&#92;&quot;unparsed&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;invalid&#92;&quot;:1},{&#92;&quot;Endpoint&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Caco-2 permeability A\u2192B&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;exact&#92;&quot;:3773,&#92;&quot;censored&#92;&quot;:31,&#92;&quot;missing&#92;&quot;:3812,&#92;&quot;unparsed&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;invalid&#92;&quot;:2},{&#92;&quot;Endpoint&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Caco-2 efflux ratio&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;exact&#92;&quot;:3777,&#92;&quot;censored&#92;&quot;:26,&#92;&quot;missing&#92;&quot;:3815,&#92;&quot;unparsed&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;invalid&#92;&quot;:0}]&quot;' data-total-rows='4' data-total-columns='6' data-max-columns='50' data-banner-text='&quot;&quot;' data-pagination='false' data-page-size='10' data-show-filters='false' data-show-download='true' data-show-search='true' data-show-column-summaries='false' data-show-data-types='true' data-show-page-size-selector='false' data-show-column-explorer='true' data-show-chart-builder='true' data-row-headers='[]' data-hidden-columns='[]' data-has-stable-row-id='false' data-lazy='false' data-preload='false'></marimo-table></marimo-ui-element><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Valid-structure analysis IDs (7,618):</strong></span></span><marimo-ui-element object-id='mMqW-1' random-id='49c76774-f20a-dc9c-8a5a-36e1e834ca60'><marimo-table data-initial-value='[]' data-label='null' data-data='&quot;[{&#92;&quot;Endpoint&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Kinetic solubility&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;exact&#92;&quot;:7298,&#92;&quot;censored&#92;&quot;:125,&#92;&quot;missing&#92;&quot;:195,&#92;&quot;unparsed&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;invalid&#92;&quot;:0},{&#92;&quot;Endpoint&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Human microsomal clearance&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;exact&#92;&quot;:4542,&#92;&quot;censored&#92;&quot;:279,&#92;&quot;missing&#92;&quot;:2796,&#92;&quot;unparsed&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;invalid&#92;&quot;:1},{&#92;&quot;Endpoint&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Caco-2 permeability A\u2192B&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;exact&#92;&quot;:3773,&#92;&quot;censored&#92;&quot;:31,&#92;&quot;missing&#92;&quot;:3812,&#92;&quot;unparsed&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;invalid&#92;&quot;:2},{&#92;&quot;Endpoint&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Caco-2 efflux ratio&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;exact&#92;&quot;:3777,&#92;&quot;censored&#92;&quot;:26,&#92;&quot;missing&#92;&quot;:3815,&#92;&quot;unparsed&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;invalid&#92;&quot;:0}]&quot;' data-total-rows='4' data-total-columns='6' data-max-columns='50' data-banner-text='&quot;&quot;' data-pagination='false' data-page-size='10' data-show-filters='false' data-show-download='true' data-show-search='true' data-show-column-summaries='false' data-show-data-types='true' data-show-page-size-selector='false' data-show-column-explorer='true' data-show-chart-builder='true' data-row-headers='[]' data-hidden-columns='[]' data-has-stable-row-id='false' data-lazy='false' data-preload='false'></marimo-table></marimo-ui-element><marimo-json-output data-json-data='{&quot;valid_molecule_ids&quot;:7618,&quot;invalid_structure_ids&quot;:[],&quot;multi_fragment_ids&quot;:[],&quot;distinct_isomeric_structures&quot;:7617,&quot;repeated_structure_groups&quot;:1,&quot;repeated_structure_ids&quot;:{&quot;Cc1c2ccnc(C(=O)N[C@H](C)CN(C)C)c2cc2c3cc(OCCCN4CCN(C)CC4)ccc3n(C)c12&quot;:[&quot;E-0001829&quot;,&quot;E-0014119&quot;]}}' data-value-types='&quot;json&quot;'></marimo-json-output></div></div><div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">For each molecule, we evaluate the <strong>set</strong> of values compatible with each reported\nobservation against inclusive gates (\u2265 or \u2264). All gates must be established passes\nto certify a pass. Any established failure rejects the molecule. Everything else\nis unresolved. Missing, malformed, or physically invalid evidence never establishes a pass.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The compatible shortlist has a lower bound equal to the established passes and an\nupper bound equal to passes plus unresolved IDs. These are logical identification\nbounds under the displayed assay evidence, not statistical confidence intervals.\nThe upper bound permits all unresolved gates to pass jointly; chemistry correlations\nmay make it loose. Experimental uncertainty beyond reported qualifiers is not modeled.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This is a descriptive analysis of a selected set of drug-discovery campaigns.\nWe do not infer that missingness is random, explain why an assay is absent, recommend\nclinical treatment, or demonstrate an improved predictive model. There is no\ntrain/test evaluation: the raw release is explored as one population.</span></span></div><div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>AI disclosure:</strong> OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex assisted with concept development, Python,\nJavaScript, testing, and explanatory text. Harsh Pandey is responsible for final\nreview and submission. The custom EvidenceBoard widget implements linked molecule\ninspection, interval bounds, and the gate-order experiment; it is developed for this notebook.\nNo synthetic measurements are substituted for the released data.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Reproduce:</strong> use a normal Python-backed molab session or run\n<code>uv run --with marimo marimo edit --sandbox missing_molecules.py</code>.\nThe file declares its dependencies. Its source is pinned and checksum verified;\na finalized copy embeds the verified raw CSV. Without embedded data it loads the\nlocal snapshot or downloads that same pinned release. Network failure is explicit.\nRDKit needs a standard Python runtime; this notebook is not advertised as WASM compatible.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Suggested reader challenge: choose two endpoint gates, find a censored observation\nthat settles a decision, then tighten the threshold until the same observation\nbecomes unresolved. Explain the change using its possible-value interval.</span></span></div></marimo-accordion>"
